Blackdrift: limit the AAB to the ABIs Blackdrift actually builds Gecko for.

Why: Blackdrift's artifact build installs GeckoView native code (libxul.so,
libmozglue.so) for one ABI only, the mozconfig --target (today arm64-v8a).
APK builds are protected by upstream's ABI splits, and the harness stages only
the arm64-v8a split. A bundle task turns those splits off, so the AAB would
also package the armeabi-v7a/x86_64 native libraries that other dependencies
ship (application-services, AndroidX) without any Gecko engine, and Google
Play would serve that broken split to 32-bit ARM and x86_64 devices.

When blackdrift/scripts/build.sh passes -PblackdriftAbiFilters (comma-separated, e.g.
arm64-v8a) to a bundle invocation, defaultConfig.ndk.abiFilters keeps only
those ABIs in the AAB. It is applied only when the invocation builds a bundle
(upstream's isAppBundle), because ndk.abiFilters may not be combined with
enabled ABI splits. Without the property nothing changes.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

diff --git a/app/build.gradle b/app/build.gradle
index 3f53a40..833829d 100644
--- a/app/build.gradle
+++ b/app/build.gradle
@@ -48,6 +48,13 @@ android {
         }
 
         vectorDrawables.useSupportLibrary = true
+
+        // Blackdrift: an AAB carries only the ABIs that have GeckoView (see the patch header).
+        if (isAppBundle && project.hasProperty("blackdriftAbiFilters")) {
+            ndk {
+                abiFilters.addAll(project.property("blackdriftAbiFilters").toString().split(",") as List)
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     bundle {
